# README sync (Alfred Identity GUI)

When you change user-visible behavior, UI tabs, config paths, build/dev workflow, or project layout, update **README.md** in the same change (or immediately after).

## What to keep in sync

- **Help section** — how to use tabs, connection modes, SSO sources, accounts, EverQuest/eqhost, tray/menu bar, updates
- **Project layout** — `internal/` packages and top-level folders
- **Config paths** — `alfred-identity/` under the OS user config dir; CSV filenames
- **Develop / build / test** commands — must match `Makefile` and `scripts/`
- **Tab list** — must match `TABS` in `frontend/src/App.jsx`

## Sources of truth

| Topic | Check |
|-------|--------|
| UI tabs & labels | `frontend/src/App.jsx` (`TABS`, connection modes, modals) |
| Config dir name | `internal/app/name.go` (`ConfigDirName`) |
| Connection modes | `internal/sources/sources.go` |
| Tray / menu actions | `internal/app/tray_*.go` |
| Version / build | `scripts/dev.sh`, `scripts/build.sh`, `.github/workflows/` |

## Do not

- Document features that exist only in the backend repo — link to `alfred-identity-backend` instead
- Leave stale tab names (e.g. listen port moved from Connections to Settings)

Keep README prose concise; prefer tables for tab/mode reference and a dedicated **Help** section for end-user steps.
